<script>(function(){var P=[["Battle of Jutland","/battle/battle-of-jutland","Battle","31 May – 1 June 1916","The British Grand Fleet under Jellicoe and the German High Seas Fleet under Scheer fought off the Danish coast of Jutland in 1916; Britain lost more ships and men, but the German fleet returned to port and stayed there."],["Battle of Hattin","/battle/battle-of-hattin","Battle","4 July 1187","On 4 July 1187 the army of the Crusader states, under King Guy of Jerusalem, was surrounded and broken near Tiberias by Saladin's forces, which then took Jerusalem and most Crusader-held towns and prompted the Third Crusade."],["Battle of Shanghai","/battle/battle-of-shanghai","Battle","13 August – 26 November 1937","China's National Revolutionary Army and Japan's Imperial Army fought for Shanghai from August to November 1937, in the Second Sino-Japanese War; Japan took the city at heavy cost to both sides and advanced on Nanjing."],["Second Battle of Panipat","/battle/second-battle-of-panipat","Battle","5 November 1556","On 5 November 1556 the Mughals under the young Akbar and his guardian Bairam Khan defeated Hemchandra Vikramaditya, known as Hemu, at Panipat, after he had taken Delhi and Agra; Hemu was captured and beheaded."],["Battle of Kohima","/battle/battle-of-kohima","Battle","4 April – 22 June 1944","A British and Indian garrison held Kohima ridge against the Japanese 31st Division in April 1944, was relieved, and with reinforcements drove the Japanese off, reopening the road to Imphal in June."],["Battle of Verdun","/battle/battle-of-verdun","Battle","21 February – 18 December 1916","The German 5th Army attacked the French defences at Verdun on the Western Front in 1916 to draw in and wear down the French army; after 302 days the French had recovered most of the ground and the Germans had failed to reach their aim."],["Battle of Trafalgar","/battle/battle-of-trafalgar","Battle","21 October 1805","A British fleet under Vice-Admiral Nelson defeated a combined French and Spanish fleet under Villeneuve off Cape Trafalgar in 1805, losing no ship, though Nelson was killed; Britain's command of the sea was not tested for over a century."],["Battle of Leuctra","/battle/battle-of-leuctra","Battle","6 July 371 BCE","The Boeotians led by the Thebans defeated Sparta and its allies at Leuctra in Boeotia on 6 July 371 BCE, after a dispute over renewing the King's Peace, and Spartan influence over Greece was shattered."],["Battle of the Bulge","/battle/battle-of-the-bulge","Battle","16 December 1944 – 25 January 1945","A German offensive through the Ardennes in Belgium and Luxembourg took the Western Allies by surprise on 16 December 1944 but was halted short of the Meuse, and the front was restored by the end of January 1945."],["Battle of Okinawa","/battle/battle-of-okinawa","Battle","1 April – 22 June 1945","United States Army and Marine Corps forces invaded Okinawa on 1 April 1945 and, after 82 days against the Japanese Thirty-Second Army, took the island at a cost that fell most heavily on its Okinawan civilians."],["Battle of Königgrätz","/battle/battle-of-koniggratz","Battle","3 July 1866","On 3 July 1866 the Prussian armies defeated the Austrian army of Ludwig von Benedek near Königgrätz in Bohemia, the decisive battle of the Austro-Prussian War, which cleared the way for a German state without Austria."],["Third Battle of Panipat","/battle/third-battle-of-panipat","Battle","14 January 1761","On 14 January 1761 the Durrani Empire and its Indian allies defeated the Maratha army at Panipat, 97 kilometres north of Delhi; tens of thousands of Marathas died in the fighting and after it."],["Battles of Lexington and Concord","/battle/battles-of-lexington-and-concord","Battle","19 April 1775","British regulars sent from Boston to seize military supplies at Concord fought Massachusetts militia at Lexington, Concord and along the road back on 19 April 1775, the first major fighting of the American Revolutionary War."],["Battle of the Trebia","/battle/battle-of-the-trebia","Battle","22 or 23 December 218 BCE","Hannibal's Carthaginian army lured a Roman army under the consul Sempronius Longus across the icy Trebia near Placentia in December 218 BCE, in the first major battle of the Second Punic War, and defeated it heavily."],["Fall of Tenochtitlan","/battle/fall-of-tenochtitlan","Battle","May – 13 August 1521","A Spanish force under Hernán Cortés and tens of thousands of Indigenous allies, above all Tlaxcalans, besieged the Mexica capital Tenochtitlan in 1521, starved it, and took it on 13 August, after which the city was sacked."],["Battle of Iwo Jima","/battle/battle-of-iwo-jima","Battle","19 February – 26 March 1945","American Marines, Navy and Army forces landed on Iwo Jima in the Volcano Islands in February 1945 and took it from the Japanese garrison under Kuribayashi in five weeks, at a cost in casualties higher than the Japanese suffered."],["Battle of Zama","/battle/battle-of-zama","Battle","202 BCE","A Roman army under Scipio Africanus defeated a Carthaginian army under Hannibal near Zama in what is now Tunisia in 202 BCE, ending the Second Punic War and leaving Carthage politically subordinate to Rome."],["Battle of Marengo","/battle/battle-of-marengo","Battle","14 June 1800","French forces under the First Consul Napoleon Bonaparte beat Michael von Melas's Austrian army near Alessandria in Piedmont on 14 June 1800 after a near defeat, and the Austrians left north-western Italy."],["Battle of Kursk","/battle/battle-of-kursk","Battle","5 July – 23 August 1943","In the summer of 1943 German forces attacked the Kursk salient on the Eastern Front, were stopped by deep Soviet defences, and were then driven back by Soviet counter-offensives that left the Red Army holding the strategic initiative."],["Battle of Austerlitz","/battle/battle-of-austerlitz","Battle","2 December 1805","Napoleon's Grande Armée defeated a combined Russian and Austrian army near Austerlitz in Moravia on 2 December 1805, in the War of the Third Coalition, and Austria then left the war by the Treaty of Pressburg."],["Battle of Mohács","/battle/battle-of-mohacs","Battle","29 August 1526","The Ottoman army under Suleiman the Magnificent defeated the Hungarian army of King Louis II near Mohács in 1526; Louis died in flight, and Hungary was later divided between the Ottomans, the Habsburgs and an eastern kingdom."],["Battle of Kadesh","/battle/battle-of-kadesh","Battle","May 1274 BCE","Ramesses II of Egypt and Muwatalli II of the Hittite Empire fought on the Orontes near Kadesh after a Hittite attack nearly broke the Egyptian army; both sides claimed victory and the Hittites kept Kadesh."],["Battle of Myriokephalon","/battle/battle-of-myriokephalon","Battle","17 September 1176","A Seljuk army under Sultan Kilij Arslan II ambushed the Byzantine army of Emperor Manuel I Komnenos in a mountain pass west of Iconium in 1176, ending Byzantine efforts to recover the Anatolian interior."],["Battle of Mikatagahara","/battle/battle-of-mikatagahara","Battle","25 January 1573","Takeda Shingen's army overran Tokugawa Ieyasu and his Oda allies on the plain of Mikatagahara in Tōtōmi Province on 25 January 1573, while Shingen marched towards Kyoto; Ieyasu escaped to Hamamatsu, and Shingen turned back."],["Battle of al-Qadisiyyah","/battle/battle-of-al-qadisiyyah","Battle","November 636","In November 636 the army of the Rashidun Caliphate defeated the Sasanian army of Rustam Farrokhzad at al-Qadisiyyah in Iraq, after which Ctesiphon fell and the Sasanians lost Mesopotamia."],["Battle of Warsaw (1920)","/battle/battle-of-warsaw-1920","Battle","August 1920","In August 1920, during the Polish–Soviet War, a Polish counterattack under Józef Piłsudski broke Mikhail Tukhachevsky's Red Army advance on Warsaw and drove it eastward, and a treaty in 1921 fixed Poland's eastern frontier."],["Battle of Poltava","/battle/battle-of-poltava","Battle","8 July 1709","A Russian army under Tsar Peter I defeated a Swedish army commanded by Carl Gustaf Rehnskiöld near Poltava in Ukraine on 8 July 1709, the largest battle of the Great Northern War; the rest of the Swedish army surrendered three days later."],["Battle of Lake Trasimene","/battle/battle-of-lake-trasimene","Battle","21 June 217 BCE","Hannibal's Carthaginian army ambushed a Roman army under the consul Gaius Flaminius on the north shore of Lake Trasimene in 217 BCE, during the Second Punic War, and killed or captured nearly all of it."],["Battle of Puebla","/battle/battle-of-puebla","Battle","5 May 1862","French troops under Charles de Lorencez failed three times to storm the Mexican forts of Loreto and Guadalupe above Puebla on 5 May 1862, during the second French intervention in Mexico, and withdrew to Orizaba to await reinforcements."],["Battle of the Yarmuk","/battle/battle-of-the-yarmuk","Battle","15 to 20 August 636","In August 636 the Rashidun Caliphate's army under Khalid ibn al-Walid defeated a larger Byzantine army under Vahan near the Yarmuk River, which ended Byzantine rule in Syria and opened the way to Egypt."],["Battle of Manzikert","/battle/battle-of-manzikert","Battle","26 August 1071","On 26 August 1071 the Seljuk army of Alp Arslan defeated the Byzantine army of Romanos IV Diogenes near Manzikert in eastern Anatolia and captured the emperor, and civil strife in Byzantium followed."],["Battle of Tsushima","/battle/battle-of-tsushima","Battle","27–28 May 1905","In the Tsushima Strait on 27–28 May 1905 the Japanese Combined Fleet under Tōgō Heihachirō destroyed or captured nearly all of the Russian Second Pacific Squadron under Rozhestvensky, and Russia sued for peace that year."],["Battle of Carrhae","/battle/battle-of-carrhae","Battle","9 June 53 BCE","A Parthian cavalry army under Surena defeated the Roman army of Marcus Licinius Crassus near Carrhae in 53 BCE; Crassus was killed, most of his men were killed or captured, and Parthia later invaded Syria and Armenia."],["Battle of Issus","/battle/battle-of-issus","Battle","5 November 333 BCE","Alexander the Great's Hellenic League army defeated the Achaemenid army of Darius III near the Pinarus river by Issus in southern Anatolia in 333 BCE, and Darius fled, leaving his family and treasury to be captured."],["Battle of the Hydaspes","/battle/battle-of-the-hydaspes","Battle","May 326 BCE","Alexander the Great's Macedonian army crossed the swollen Hydaspes in May 326 BCE and defeated the Pauravas under Porus on its bank in what is now Punjab, Pakistan; Alexander spared Porus and made him a satrap."],["Battle of Badr","/battle/battle-of-badr","Battle","13 March 624 CE","On 13 March 624 CE (17 Ramadan, 2 AH) Muhammad's followers from Medina defeated a larger Qurayshi army from Mecca near Badr, killing several Meccan leaders and strengthening Muhammad's position."],["Battle of the Catalaunian Plains","/battle/battle-of-the-catalaunian-plains","Battle","20 June 451 CE","A coalition led by the Roman general Aetius and the Visigothic king Theodoric I fought the Huns and their vassals under Attila in Gaul in 451 CE; Theodoric was killed, Attila withdrew, and the outcome is disputed."],["Battle of Boyacá","/battle/battle-of-boyaca","Battle","7 August 1819","A combined Venezuelan and New Granadan army with a British Legion under Simón Bolívar defeated Colonel José María Barreiro's Spanish III Division at Boyacá in 1819, opening the road to Santa Fe and the founding of Gran Colombia."],["Battle of the Somme","/battle/battle-of-the-somme","Battle","1 July – 18 November 1916","British Empire and French armies attacked the German Second Army on both sides of the upper Somme from 1 July to 18 November 1916, gaining about 10 km at a cost of over a million casualties."],["Battle of Alarcos","/battle/battle-of-alarcos","Battle","18 July 1195","The Almohad caliph Abu Yusuf Ya'qub al-Mansur defeated King Alfonso VIII of Castile at Alarcos, near the Guadiana, on 18 July 1195, and Castile's field army was destroyed, leaving the road to Toledo open."],["Battle of Vienna (1683)","/battle/battle-of-vienna-1683","Battle","12 September 1683","On 12 September 1683 a relief army of Imperial and Polish forces under John III Sobieski defeated the Ottoman army of Kara Mustafa Pasha at Vienna, after a two-month siege, and the Ottomans were later driven from most of Hungary."],["Battle of Sagrajas","/battle/battle-of-sagrajas","Battle","23 October 1086","An Almoravid army under Yusuf ibn Tashfin, joined by the taifa kings of al-Andalus, defeated Alfonso VI of Castile near Badajoz in October 1086, easing Christian pressure on the taifas and opening the way for Almoravid rule in al-Andalus."],["Battle of Marignano","/battle/battle-of-marignano","Battle","13–14 September 1515","Francis I of France, with German landsknechts and late-arriving Venetian allies, defeated the Swiss Confederacy near Melegnano, south-east of Milan, in September 1515; the Perpetual Peace of 1516 followed."],["Battle of the Little Bighorn","/battle/battle-of-the-little-bighorn","Battle","25–26 June 1876","On the Little Bighorn River in Montana Territory, Lakota, Northern Cheyenne and Arapaho forces defeated the 7th Cavalry under Lieutenant Colonel Custer in June 1876, the most significant action of the Great Sioux War, which the United States still won."],["Battle of Sedan (1870)","/battle/battle-of-sedan-1870","Battle","1 to 2 September 1870","Prussian and allied German armies under Moltke surrounded the French Army of Châlons at Sedan in the Franco-Prussian War, forced its surrender with Napoleon III on 2 September 1870, and the Second Empire fell two days later."],["Fall of Singapore","/battle/fall-of-singapore","Battle","8 to 15 February 1942","Japanese forces under General Tomoyuki Yamashita crossed the Johor Strait and took Singapore from the British garrison under Lieutenant-General Arthur Percival, who surrendered on 15 February 1942 in the Second World War."],["Battle of Guandu","/battle/battle-of-guandu","Battle","200 CE","In 200 CE, late in the Eastern Han dynasty, the warlord Cao Cao held the fortified camp at Guandu against the larger army of Yuan Shao, burned Yuan's grain at Wuchao and routed him, becoming the dominant power in northern China."],["Battle of Leipzig","/battle/battle-of-leipzig","Battle","16–19 October 1813","The armies of the Sixth Coalition, from Austria, Prussia, Sweden and Russia, defeated Napoleon's Grande Armée at Leipzig in Saxony over four days in October 1813, and the French withdrew to France."],["Battle of Yamen","/battle/battle-of-yamen","Battle","19 March 1279","A Yuan fleet under Zhang Hongfan defeated the chained Song fleet in the bay at Yamen in southern China on 19 March 1279, ending the Song dynasty; the child emperor Zhao Bing died in the sea."],["Siege of Jerusalem (1099)","/battle/siege-of-jerusalem-1099","Battle","7 June – 15 July 1099","Crusaders from Western Europe besieged Fatimid-held Jerusalem from 7 June to 15 July 1099, took it by assault with siege towers and a ram, massacred thousands of its people, and soon founded the Kingdom of Jerusalem."],["Battle of Sekigahara","/battle/battle-of-sekigahara","Battle","21 October 1600 (Keichō 5, 15th day of the 9th month)","On 21 October 1600 the forces of Tokugawa Ieyasu defeated a coalition led by Ishida Mitsunari in what is now Gifu Prefecture after several commanders defected; Ieyasu became shōgun in 1603."],["Battle of Adrianople","/battle/battle-of-adrianople","Battle","9 August 378","Gothic rebels under Fritigern defeated the Eastern Roman army and killed the emperor Valens near Adrianople in Thrace in 378, during the Gothic War of 376 to 382."],["Battle of Agincourt","/battle/battle-of-agincourt","Battle","25 October 1415","On 25 October 1415 Henry V's English army, marching to Calais and heavily outnumbered, defeated a French army near Azincourt in northern France, a victory that gave England the advantage in the Hundred Years' War for some years."],["Battle of Waterloo","/battle/battle-of-waterloo","Battle","18 June 1815","On 18 June 1815 a French army under Napoleon was defeated near Waterloo, in present-day Belgium, by a British-led army under Wellington and a Prussian army under Blücher; Napoleon abdicated again four days later."],["Battle of Jena–Auerstedt","/battle/battle-of-jena-auerstedt","Battle","14 October 1806","On 14 October 1806 Napoleon's army defeated Prince Hohenlohe's Prussians at Jena while Marshal Davout's single corps beat the main Prussian army at Auerstedt, in the War of the Fourth Coalition; Prussia's resistance collapsed in the weeks after."],["Battle of Kosovo","/battle/battle-of-kosovo","Battle","15 June 1389","An Ottoman army under Sultan Murad I fought an army led by the Serbian Prince Lazar Hrebeljanović on the Kosovo field in 1389; both leaders died, both armies were badly weakened, and the Serbian principalities later became Ottoman vassals."],["Battle of the Nile","/battle/battle-of-the-nile","Battle","1–3 August 1798","A British fleet under Rear-Admiral Sir Horatio Nelson attacked the French fleet of Vice-admiral Brueys anchored in Aboukir Bay, Egypt, in August 1798, and destroyed or captured all but four of its ships, leaving Napoleon's army in Egypt cut off."],["Normandy landings","/battle/normandy-landings","Battle","6 June 1944","On 6 June 1944 American, British and Canadian forces, with airborne troops and a fleet drawn from eight navies, landed on five beaches on the Normandy coast, opening the liberation of France and Western Europe."],["Battle on the Ice","/battle/battle-on-the-ice","Battle","5 April 1242","The united forces of Novgorod and Vladimir-Suzdal under Prince Alexander Nevsky defeated the Livonian Order and the Bishopric of Dorpat under Bishop Hermann of Dorpat at Lake Peipus on 5 April 1242, a battle later made a Russian national symbol."],["Battle of the Plains of Abraham","/battle/battle-of-the-plains-of-abraham","Battle","13 September 1759","British troops under James Wolfe defeated French regulars and Canadian militia under the Marquis de Montcalm outside Quebec City on 13 September 1759, during the Seven Years' War; the city capitulated five days later."]],d=Math.floor(Date.now()/864e5),p=P[d%P.length],a=document.getElementById("hub-pick");if(a){a.href=p[1];var im=document.createElement("img");im.src="/logos/thumbs/"+encodeURIComponent(p[0]).replace(/'/g,"%27")+".png";im.alt="";im.width=64;im.height=64;a.querySelector(".hub-pick-img").appendChild(im);a.querySelector(".hub-pick-k").textContent="Today\u2019s pick \u00b7 "+p[2]+(p[3]?" \u00b7 "+p[3]:"");a.querySelector(".hub-pick-n").textContent=p[0];a.querySelector(".hub-pick-d").textContent=p[4];}var b=document.getElementById("hub-surprise"),P=["/battle/"];if(b)b.addEventListener("click",function(){function go(){if(typeof SEARCH_PROFILES==="undefined")return;var a=SEARCH_PROFILES.filter(function(r){return P.some(function(p){return r[1].indexOf(p)===0})});if(a.length)location.href=a[Math.floor(Math.random()*a.length)][1]}if(typeof SEARCH_PROFILES!=="undefined")return go();var sc=document.createElement("script");sc.src=(typeof SEARCH_PROFILES_SRC!=="undefined"?SEARCH_PROFILES_SRC:"/search-profiles.js");sc.onload=go;sc.onerror=go;document.head.appendChild(sc)});})();</script>
